Package: flickos-style-eleven
Architecture: all
# flickos-layouts 1.67 and flickos-menu 1.22: Menu=bottom-center, the start
# menu above the middle of the panel; flickos-layouts 1.68: Use replaces a
# menu daemon still running the code from before the upgrade; 1.69: the
# flickos/weather placeholder (the weather at the left end while it is on);
# gnome-themes-extra-data, adwaita-icon-theme and fonts-open-sans: the GTK
# theme (Adwaita-dark), the
# icons and the panel's font Eleven names; adwaita-icon-theme-legacy:
# Adwaita's full-color icons for apps that name an older icon, which
# otherwise fall back to a dark grey symbolic one (Adwaita only recommends
# it, and FlickOS installs no recommends).
Depends: flickos-layouts (>= 1.69),
         flickos-menu (>= 1.22),
         gnome-themes-extra-data,
         adwaita-icon-theme,
         adwaita-icon-theme-legacy,
         fonts-open-sans,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Eleven style and layout for the FlickOS desktop
 A dark style for FlickOS: neutral dark grey windows and title bars with
 wide, flat buttons in thin lines and a close button that turns red under
 the pointer, a sky blue accent, a near-black terminal, and folds of blue
 light on a deep blue wallpaper with FlickOS's halo.
 .
 Its layout has one see-through dark panel at the bottom with the apps
 button and the open windows in the middle, and the status icons and a
 two-line clock at the right. The start menu opens above the middle of the
 panel.
 .
 Installing it adds Eleven to Desktop Layout & Style; Software's Use sets
 the style and the layout together.
